BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Preservation Hall Jazz Band: Creole Christmas
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261218T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261218T211500
UID:af31f66352f0e77dcd19dbc3098523a5@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/c059
 808/2147483647/strip/true/crop/447x447+0+0/resize/254x254!/quality/90/?url
 =https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fec%2F25%2Fa69f27ae4f0fb28
 982f844465311%2Fimage-2.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Buskirk-Chumley Theater\nGet in the holiday spiri
 t with a New Orleans twist!\n The Preservation Hall Jazz Band brings their
  beloved Creole Christmas to Bloomington! Join as the band performs New Or
 leans classics as well as some of our best-loved holiday selections with a
  twist.\n The group derives its name from Preservation Hall\, the venerabl
 e music venue located in the heart of New Orleans’ French Quarter\, foun
 ded in 1961 by Allan and Sandra Jaffe. They’ve traveled worldwide spread
 ing their mission to nurture and perpetuate the art form of New Orleans Ja
 zz. Whether performing at Carnegie Hall or Lincoln Center\, for British Ro
 yalty or the King of Thailand\, this music embodies a joyful\, timeless sp
 irit. Under the auspices of current director\, Ben Jaffe\, the son of foun
 ders Allan and Sandra\, Preservation Hall continues with a deep reverence 
 and consciousness of its greatest attributes in the modern day as a venue
 \, band\, and record label.\n The PHJB began touring in 1963 and for many 
 years there were several bands successfully touring under the name Preserv
 ation Hall. Many of the band’s charter members performed with the pionee
 rs who invented jazz in the early twentieth century including Buddy Bolden
 \, Jelly Roll Morton\, Louis Armstrong\, and Bunk Johnson. Band leaders ov
 er the band’s history include the brothers Willie and Percy Humphrey\, h
 usband and wife Billie and De De Pierce\, famed pianist Sweet Emma Barrett
 \, and in the modern day Wendall and John Brunious. These founding artists
  and dozens of others passed on the lessons of their music to a younger ge
 neration who now follow in their footsteps like the current lineup.\nTicke
 ts: https://buskirkchumley.org/events/preservation-hall-jazz-band-creole-c
 hristmas-december-18-2026/
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington\, Indi
 ana 47408
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/preservation-hall-jazz-ba
 nd-creole-christmas-10-10-2026-13-00-26
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
