BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“The Snowy Day” – Music by Joel Thompson\; Libretto by Andre
 a Davis Pinkney
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270205T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270205T235900
UID:3f97a3216e4955b65e1a31f926a5e405@ipm.org
DESCRIPTION:The Snowy Day\nMusic by Joel Thompson\nLibretto by Andrea Davi
 s Pinkney\n SNOW BALL\n A young boy wakes to find his world magically tran
 sformed overnight—blanketed in fresh\, glittering snow. Ezra Jack Keats
 ’ 1962 book is a joyful\, wonder-filled adventure through the city stree
 ts that became an equally delightful opera: the tale of Peter’s first sn
 ow day on his own.\n In 2016\, Andrea Davis Pinkney’s libretto started a
 s an homage to that book—a poem entitled A Poem for Peter. Then composer
  Joel Thompson\, who had already gained attention for his choral work Seve
 n Last Words of the Unarmed\, brought accessibility and emotionally rich m
 usical language to this children’s opera.\n The Snowy Day had its world 
 premiere in 2021\, produced by Houston Grand Opera\, following a long traj
 ectory of a book that featured a Black child as its hero at a time when su
 ch representation in children’s literature was rare.\n An Opera in One A
 ct Based on The Snowy Day\, a book by Ezra Jack Keats\n Commissioned by th
 e Houston Grand Opera\nPremiered by Houston Grand Opera in December 2021\n
 Original Production directed by Omer Ben Seadia\n Artistic Staff\nConducto
 r\nJoseph Young\n Stage Director and Choreographer\nEboni Adams\n Set Desi
 gner\nAmy Rubin\n Costume Designer\nJessica Jahn\n Wig & Makeup Designer\n
 Andrew Elliot\nTickets: https://am.ticketmaster.com/iumac/buy
LOCATION:Musical Arts Center\, 201 S. Eagleson Ave\, Bloomington\, Indiana
  47405
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/the-snowy-day-music-by-jo
 el-thompson-libretto-by-andrea-davis-pinkney-13-11-2026-14-53-47
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
