BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stardust Turns 100: A Celebration of Hoagy Carmichael
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270213T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270213T235900
UID:51dc894b94c9d9605696c79312483cbf@ipm.org
DESCRIPTION:Bloomington native and IU alumnus Hoagy Carmichael wrote his l
 egendary “Stardust” in 1927\, recording it at the fabled Gennett Recor
 ds in Richmond\, Indiana: the first of its over 1\,500 recordings and the 
 first of his 50 hit records. This season\, the Singing Hoosiers and the Ja
 zz Studies Department join forces to celebrate the centenary of this iconi
 c song and the man who wrote it.\nTickets: https://am.ticketmaster.com/ium
 ac/buy
LOCATION:Musical Arts Center\, 201 S. Eagleson Ave\, Bloomington\, Indiana
  47405
