DESCRIPTION:Presented by IU Auditorium\nMarking the fifth production in th
 e Jazz at Lincoln Center PRESENTS series\, guest vocalists Kate Kortum and
  David Marino will debut arrangements of tunes from Broadway’s most belo
 ved productions including Hamilton\, Wicked\, South Pacific\, West Side St
 ory\, and more in a special concert event entitled World on a String: Swin
 ging Songs of Broadway.\n For over three decades\, Jazz at Lincoln Center 
 has been a leading advocate for jazz\, culture\, and arts education global
 ly. Under the direction of Wynton Marsalis\, Jazz at Lincoln Center has br
 ought the art form of jazz from the heart of New York City to over 446 cit
 ies in more than 40 countries.\nTickets: https://www.iuauditorium.com/even
 ts/detail/jalc-2027
LOCATION:IU Auditorium\, 1211 East 7th Street\, Bloomington\, Indiana 4740
 5
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/jazz-at-lincoln-center-pr
 esents-world-on-a-string-swinging-songs-of-broadway-05-08-2026-13-04-23
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
